UID:TKF/6755f42da02aaf1c2599e7ae/22010/29826660/0/0
DTSTART:20260916T230000Z
DTEND:20260917T000000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/22010/1789599600000
SUMMARY: Things Fall Apart: In Conversation with Allison Glenn\, Curator\
 , Toronto Biennial of Art 2026
DESCRIPTION:Things Fall Apart: In Conversation with Allison Glenn\, Curat
 or\, Toronto Biennial of Art 2026\n\nJoin us!\n\nSeptember 16\, 2026\n7:0
 0pm\n100 McCaul Street\, Auditorium (Room 190)\nOCAD University\n\nFREE: 
 Get your ticket here https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/in-conversation-with-all
 ison-glenn-curator-2026-toronto-biennial-of-art-tickets-1999034475930?aff
 =oddtdtcreator\n\nThe fourth edition of the Toronto Biennial of Art https
 ://torontobiennial.org/ \, Things Fall Apart\, curated by Allison Glenn h
 ttps://www.allisonglenn.com/ \, unfolds through a set of propositions anc
 hored by the question: What can we learn from artists who explore rupture
  as an ontological tool or a way of understanding?\n\nRelying on the shar
 ed geographies of the Great Lakes as a place of departure\, this Biennial
  traces relationships between the expansive but interconnected waters of 
 the Great Lakes region and over sixteen global waterways that span five c
 ontinents.Things Fall Apart considers ideas of syncopation and disruption
  through the lens of shared thematics that emerged from artists’ voices: 
 diaspora through movement and migration\, syncretic traditions\, notions 
 of borders\, water networks\, maritime histories of empire\, corporeality
 \, calls to action\, global climate justice\, genocides\, speculative and
  science fictions\, material memory\, the transformation of knowledge\, a
 nd both water and land as conceptual links.\n\nThings Fall Apart is organ
 ized in three parts: a central exhibition that grounds itself in methodol
 ogies of collectivity\, sovereignty\, reflection\, and refusal\; a series
  of performances and artist-led programming that invites embodied engagem
 ent with these practices\; and a collaboratively curated gathering. Join 
 this year's curator to learn about the process of leading to Things Fall 
 Apart.\n\n\nAllison Glenn:\n\nAllison Glenn is a New York-based curator a
 nd writer focusing on the intersection of art and public space\, through 
 biennials\, special projects\, public art\, & major new commissions. For 
 seventeen years\, Glenn has been devoted to realizing ambitious and exper
 imental exhibitions with a wide range of contemporary artists working acr
 oss the globe. She is Curator of the 2026 Toronto Biennial of Art\, title
 d Things Fall Apart\, opening September 26\, 2026\, and Curator of Espaci
 o Central\, as part of the CARA Platform.
CATEGORIES:Art-Show/Gallery-Event,In-Conversation,OCAD-University
