DTSTART:20261001T223000Z
DTEND:20261002T000000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/22011/1790893800000
SUMMARY: Zahra Ahooei: Film Screening & Conversation
DESCRIPTION:Join Iranian filmmaker Zahra Ahooei\, for a screening and con
 versation about her award-winning short films and her current documentary
  project\, HouseLight.\n\nFREE (by Ticket only): ZAHRA AHOOEI OCAD FILM S
 CREENING TICKETS https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/zahra-ahooei-film-screening-
 conversation-october-1-2026-tickets-1999296660130?aff=oddtdtcreator\n\nOc
 tober 1\, 2026\n6:30-8:00pm\nOCAD University\, 100 McCaul Street\nAuditor
 ium (Room 190)\n\nZahra Ahooei is an Iranian filmmaker\, writer\, and med
 ia artist currently based in Canada. She has directed several short narra
 tive films\, including Reflex (2024)\, Prestige (2020)\, Sign Out (2017)\
 , and Extra Time (2015)\, which have been screened internationally and re
 cognized with various awards. Her background also includes years of exper
 ience in journalism\, television writing\, and content creation for both 
 broadcast and digital platforms.\n\nZahra’s upcoming project\, HouseLight
 \, is a feature-length documentary that employs a non-fiction storytellin
 g approach. Rooted in her personal experiences\, the film explores themes
  of loss\, memory\, and immigration through a distinctly female perspecti
 ve. In 2024\, Zahra developed this project during her participation in th
 e Newcomer Filmmentor program at the Liaison of Independent Filmmakers of
  Toronto (LIFT).\n\nShe is currently an IIE Artist Protection Fund Fellow
  in residence at OCAD University\, which acts as the primary host and cre
 ative hub for the development and production of her ongoing film project.
  As part of this fellowship network\, OBORO\, an artist-run centre in Mon
 treal dedicated to the presentation and production of visual\, media\, an
 d digital arts will also host Zahra during the later stages of the projec
 t in collaboration with APF and OCAD University.\n\nIn November 2025\, wh
 ile still in development\, HouseLight was selected to participate in Doc 
 Lab Montreal’s feature film program\, part of Forum RIDM\, the industry p
 latform of the Montreal International Documentary Festival (RIDM)\, one o
 f North America’s leading documentary events fostering creative exchange\
 , professional development\, and international co-productions.
CATEGORIES:Film,OCAD-University,In-Conversation
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6a99a2c688c0f34940696cc7/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Join Iranian filmmaker Zahra Ahooei\, for a screenin
 g and conversation about her award-winning short films and her current do
 cumentary project\, HouseLight....
LOCATION:OCAD University Auditorium\,100 McCaul St\, Toronto\, ON M5T 2W7
 \, Canada
